 "A frame holding a NaN: Unbound's x angle is a NaN with the sign bit set, the Editor's has none. In Unbound the sign comes from negating the arcsine of the rotation's NaN: x's sign bit is the inverse of the sign of the rotation's y (a positive NaN for this frame), whatever the sign of z. Whether the Editor's rotation of such a matrix holds a y of the other sign or its angle step treats a NaN otherwise is not isolated: the bits of Matrix4x4.rotation are measured for finite matrices only (tests/projects/floatrounding native/matrixDecompose; follow-up: an Editor control of the sign of y in Matrix4x4.rotation for a matrix holding a NaN, which separates the two)": [
